    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Three patterns after ten",
      "texto": "11 to 15 are new words: **once, doce, trece, catorce, quince**.\n\n16 to 19 join diez with the unit, and they keep an accent: **dieciséis, diecisiete, dieciocho, diecinueve**.\n\n21 to 29 are one word, with an accent on the unit: **veintiuno, veintidós, veintitrés**. From 30, the ten and the unit are separate, with **y**: treinta y uno, cuarenta y dos, cincuenta y tres.\n\nThe tens: veinte, treinta, cuarenta, cincuenta, sesenta, setenta, ochenta, noventa, **cien**."
    },
